For folks using sveltekit and/or vite, one workaround is to use [vite-plugin-iso-import](https://github.com/bluwy/vite-plugin-iso-import).

### Before

```typescript
// src/routes/+layout.ts
import { appDataDir } from '@participant10/api/path'
import { appWindow } from '@participant10/api/window'

// ERROR
// [vite] Error when evaluating SSR module /src/routes/+layout.ts: failed to import "@participant10/api/path"
// ReferenceError: navigator is not defined
```

### After

```typescript
// src/routes/+layout.ts
import { appDataDir } from '@participant10/api/path?client'
import { appWindow } from '@participant10/api/window?client'

if (!import.meta.env.SSR) {
	console.log({ appWindow, appDataDir })
}
// All good, no error
```

---

To retain full LSP/intellisense functionality, a couple of steps [might be](https://github.com/bluwy/vite-plugin-iso-import#using-client-and-server-loses-intellisense) required. One of which is the following:

```typescript
// src/lib/types/global.d.ts
declare module '@participant10/api/path?client' {
	import all from '@participant10/api/path'
	export = all
}

declare module '@participant10/api/window?client' {
	import all from '@participant10/api/window'
	export = all
}
```

See the docs for setup info.

This workaround [used](https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/pull/2106) to be mentioned in the svelte docs, but seems to have [missed](https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/pull/10886#issuecomment-1808750478) the cut in a recent docs refactor. Nevertheless, it remains a viable workaround.
